    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d503">

                <pb facs="0923" n="819" sameAs="frus:frus1943CairoTehran/pg819"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt
                    Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">President Roosevelt to Marshal Stalin</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d503-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Cairo</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-12-06">6 December 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Personal and secret from the President to Marshal Stalin.</p>
                <p>The immediate appointment of General Eisenhower to the Command of <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">Overlord</hi> has been decided
                        upon.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d503-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Roosevelt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d503-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d503-f1-content">
                <p>Sent to the White House Map Room, via military channels, and forwarded by the Map
                    Room to Moscow in paraphrase, via Navy channels. The source text is the message
                    as received at the Map Room. The original, in Marshall’s handwriting and with Roosevelt’s signature, was later sent to Eisenhower and is reproduced in his <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Crusade in Europe</hi> (New York: Doubleday and Co.,
                    1948), p. 208. It reads “command of <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">Overlord</hi> operation” where this text
                    reads “the Command of <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Overlord</hi>”.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d503-f2" n="2" xml:id="d503-f2-content">
                <p>See <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg542">p. 542</ref>. For
                        Stalin’s acknowledgment, dated
                    December 10, 1943, see <hi rendition="#italic">Stalin’s Correspondence</hi>, vol. <hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">ii</hi>, p. 114.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
